{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21229-demon-the-descent-prestige-edition-cheaper-than-dtrpg-pod-w-discount","id":21229,"title":"\"Demon: the Descent\" Prestige Edition cheaper than DTRPG PoD w/ discount?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-01T11:38:08-08:00","id":21229,"title":"\"Demon: the Descent\" Prestige Edition cheaper than DTRPG PoD w/ discount?","content":"So, for the $50 &quot;Unchained (US)&quot; (<i>or $75 &quot;Unchained (Non-US)</i>), you get the Prestige Edition of &quot;Demon: the Descent&quot; PDF and a hard cover book with an image printed on a metallic under layer, and featuring an emboss/deboss of the logo and mirror cracks, estimated to be about 400 pages, with a two-color interior (black and blue) and endpapers on high quality paper stock. That's just the physical book itself, and not any other stretch goal add-ons.<br /> <br /> Now... at $110K, the &quot;PoD Discount&quot; was reached, meaning that each person who orders a Prestige Edition will be able to purchase a PoD of the book &quot;at, or near cost&quot;. However, unless you plan to get a b/w hardcover, (especially if you live within the US)<b> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">it may still be cheaper to purchase multiple copies of the Prestige Edition for $45 each <span style=\"font-size:12px\">(or $75 for Non-US)</span>.</span></b> <br /> Right now, the 530 page <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/94815/Vampire-The-Masquerade-20th-Anniversary-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">V20</a> and <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/112871/Werewolf-The-Apocalypse-20th-Anniversary-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">W20</a> are $50/$65/$90 [<span style=\"color:#696969\"><i>(b/w)/(standard color)/(premium color)</i></span>] and 400 page <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/111598/Mummy-the-Curse\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a> is X/$35/$60, so it'll probably be around $40 for B/W (if it's offered), $50 for &quot;Standard Color&quot;, and $75 for &quot;Premium Color&quot;.<br /> <br /> Standard Color gives you color, but, well, it's inkjet printing, so the color isn't very vibrant, it's dull, and there's banding issues sometimes... and Premium, well, would have to be half of the price of Retail to make it about the same price as the $45 add-on.<br /> <br /> Now, this gets mucked up when you consider <i>international shipping prices</i>... so take all of that into consideration ($70 extra for each Deluxe Edition add-on, plus any other taxes per book means that it may be easier to have it printed in Europe and shipped.) Those of you who are used to these sorts of purchases will have your own experiences to base your decision on.<br /> <br /> I just thought I'd point this out for folks to consider and discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T18:20:06-08:00","id":21376,"title":"","content":"Well yes, that's likely the case. But the difference is. With the PoD as well. We can have a tangible book in our hands that much sooner. I've been weighing adding another book to my pledge or adding another PoD to purchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}